{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And he hewed.</b> It is the usage of the language to speak thus: 'and he took in his hand two stone tablets' (Exodus 34:4), and it does not say 'and he took in his hand the two tablets,' just as 'and YHWH rained upon Sodom and upon Gomorrah brimstone and fire from before YHWH' (Genesis 19:24), and it does not say 'from before Him,' and likewise in one verse 'the children of Israel' five times, and this is a path of eloquence."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:09.589048772Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}